{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And the festival of harvest.</b> It is the festival of Shavuot." "<b>First-fruits of your labors.</b> For it is the time of bringing first-fruits — the two loaves that come on Atzeret would permit the new grain for meal-offerings and for bringing first-fruits to the Temple, as it says ״וּבְיוֹם הַבִּכּוּרִים״ etc. (Numbers 28)." "<b>And the festival of ingathering.</b> It is the festival of Sukkot." "<b>When you gather in your labors.</b> For all the days of the sun the produce dries in the fields, and on the festival they gather it into the house because of the rains."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:08.234542793Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}